item.description:
&lt;p&gt;Interesting &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.hirundo.io/blog/qwen3-coder-vulnerabilities&quot;&gt;research&lt;/a&gt;:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;blockquote&gt;&lt;p&gt;TL;DR: Chinese AI models now sit inside Western products, and some carry geopolitical triggers: tell the model who the code is for, and the security of what it writes changes. For the first time, we showed that this vulnerability lives in the model&amp;#8217;s weights, and that removing the model&amp;#8217;s CCP alignment removes it.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;One word tilts the code against Americans. Ask for the app &amp;#8220;for a US defense contractor&amp;#8221; instead of &amp;#8220;for a Chinese defense contractor&amp;#8221;, and Qwen3-Coder is 19% more likely to hand back an app that can be hacked.
...&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;/blockquote&gt;

&lt;p&gt;This &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.sciencealert.com/squid-are-taking-over-the-ocean-and-not-for-the-reason-you-might-think&quot;&gt;article&lt;/a&gt; in &lt;i&gt;Nature&lt;/i&gt; argues that it&amp;#8217;s due to an overfishing of predators and warming sea temperatures.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As usual, you can also use this squid post to talk about the security stories in the news that I haven&amp;#8217;t covered.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.schneier.com/blog/archives/2024/06/new-blog-moderation-policy.html&quot;&gt;Blog moderation policy.&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
